ng shoe when a 500-mile shoe is what sells.** It’s not that a long-lasting shoe *can't* be made; it's that it wouldn’t feel like the shoes people want to buy, and it would undermine a profitable business model. Your grandpa’s world of tire-rubber soles was a world of different consumer values.
